If HARD is not defined, all wands of wishing are created with 3 charges.
If HARD is defined, then wand will have up to 3 charges.
A WoW can be recharged exactly once, again, up to 3 charges.
If the scroll is blessed, it will charge the wand to exactly 3. [unless
the wand was at 3 already, then the wand explodes].
If the scroll is not blessed or cursed, it will charge the wand by one.
[unless the wand was at 3 already, then you just use up a recharge]
After charges are exhasted, the wand can give a final last wish and
disintegrate.  Wands can be found from previous adventurers that have
already been recharged, already zapped, etc. Therefore,

1. Finding an unrecharged wand, it can start with 3,2,1 or 0 charges.
   If it has 0 charges and you zap it, it will disintegrate and you
   can't recharge it.  In this case, you get only one wish.  Recharging
   the wand will give you, depending on circumstances, a wand with
   3,2,1, or 0 charges.  So, an unrecharged wand can give up to 7
   wishes (if it started at 3).  If you foolishly zap it at 0 charges,
   you get only one wish.  If it started at just 0 and you recharged
   with an uncursed scroll, you get a total of two wishes.

2. Finding a recharged wand, it can start with 3,2,1, or 0 charges.  In
   this case, you can never recharge again and simply get 4,3,2, or 1
   wish.

3. If your luck is not good enough, wishes may fail.
